From 53e2d620b66642413cdb1c2a71d21654a8dc0b9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:05:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sessions): let a list leave automated rows out before
 paging

Follow-up to the paged Archived view. On 2026-11-17 the Archived view's
first 500-row page held 92 of the user's own chats; the rest were
auto-archived bot runs from the mini's bb-* profiles (15,432 of 16,899
archived rows), which the sidebar then hid. The same rows are what made
a page slow: the Desktop reads each registry backend 100 rows per
request, so 500 bot rows per profile is five round trips each, and a
deeper page re-reads that prefix.

Why it was not caught: "automated" was only ever a stamp on rows already
fetched, so no list could be sized or counted without them.

- backend: /api/sessions and /api/profiles/sessions take
  automated=exclude. Per store, automated_listing_exclusion() turns the
  profile's own policy into SQL: a "*" profile contributes nothing;
  otherwise every source spelling the store holds that the automated
  stamp would flag is excluded, so filter and stamp agree row for row.
  Rows and total both shrink. The policy is part of the all-profiles
  scan cache key, since config.yaml changes without a state.db write.
  Default stays "include".
- desktop: the sidebar's Archived cursor sends automated=exclude while
  "Show automated & test sessions" is off, and the view starts over at
  one page when that preference flips. A backend that predates the
  option ignores it; its rows are still hidden client-side as before.
  Settings > Archived sessions still lists every archived row.

Behaviour to know: with the option on, a pinned or needs-attention
automated row is left out too (the live sidebar keeps those); turning
"Show automated & test sessions" on lists them.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_sessions_automated_exclude.py (both routes,
"*" profile, explicit sources, other-case spelling, interactive
allowlist, combined with exclude_sources, live list, pinned row, policy
change without a db write, invalid value, no policy);
sidebar-archive.test.ts (filter sent / not sent, restart on flip, no
fetch while closed); sessions-settings.test.tsx (settings asks for every
row); api/sessions.test.ts (query string);
profile-session-routing.test.ts (the merge already forwards query
params to the primary and registry backends; this pins it).

Not measured end to end: the page time in the app, which needs all three
gateways on this code. Measured on this Mac's store in-process: the
archived list is 0.4 s warm either way, so the 12 s was the fan-out, not
the query. Not changed: registry backends are still read 100 rows per
request, and a deeper page still re-reads its prefix.

